From e4fd7587390a189fa2726896a7809979858d1e2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:19:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sync): remove per-round macOS power-probe forks [daveey]

Why: the never-ending kanban sync executor item calls host_fully_awake
once per round. Its pmset/ioreg subprocesses fork the large multithreaded
Mac gateway; the owner measured about42ms calling-thread CPU per spawn,
explaining the roughly2%-core residual. Submission/completion scopes
cannot publish a never-ending item's remainder until it returns.

Read current power assertions, providing power source and clamshell via
IOKit/CoreFoundation. Cache only ABI bindings, never the verdict: preserve
DarkWake semantics, error-is-awake policy, and CLI fallback if the native
ABI is unavailable. All sync/tick/cron callers use the shared entry point.
Use a residual sync.round/loop scope per completed iteration so nested
board passes retain their CPU and the ongoing executor's remainder is
named before shutdown. No scheduling, deadlines or active streams cached.

Also pass only the operation's own exception to diagnostic Scope.__exit__,
not an ambient caller exception. Pin real error booking and malformed
WorkItem fallback (the retained R5/I4 review gaps).

Proof:
- Baseline round/ambient tests RED:2 failed,1 passed.
- Baseline native-route tests RED:4 failed,1 passed.
-32 directly importing/reference suites:748 passed,0 failed,14 skipped.
- Full staged scripts/check --base origin/main passed.
-19 exact-anchor mutants killed; final baseline57 passed/1 skipped.
  The initial number-type survivor exposed a masked fixture; the strengthened
  active-assertion control kills it before the independent lid guard.
- Native ABI/error/release policy unit tests and a macOS-only real native
  smoke test; actual macOS execution and post-deploy CPU gates remain owed.
- Real executor remains pending during snapshot; real board Pass and Scope
  both retain their names/CPU without double booking.
- Apple pmset.m show_assertions_system_aggregates prints the raw integer;
  PMAssertions.c copyAggregateValuesDictionary/getAssertionLevel supplies
  0/1. This is distinct from individual assertion-level constants.

Live acceptance remains on t_eeeeee0000000019: natural deployment only,
>=3000s uptime, idle same-process snapshot window; run_forever-thread
residual<0.1%core, round overhead<5ms, pool unnamed share<5%. No live
CPU improvement is claimed by the offline tests.
